Standard Operating Procedure – Centrifuge Operation
Document ID: SOP-CT-04
Version: 1.2
Effective Date: 03/03/2025

Purpose:
To outline the correct procedure for operating the Model X200 centrifuge to ensure consistent and safe sample processing.

Scope:
This SOP applies to all laboratory staff trained in instrument handling.

Procedure:
1. Inspect rotor for cracks or residue before use.
2. Balance all tubes to within ±0.05 g.
3. Set speed according to the sample matrix (default: 4500 RPM).
4. Ensure the lid is fully locked before starting the run.
5. Allow the rotor to come to a complete stop before opening the lid.
6. Record run parameters in the digital logbook.

Safety Notes:
- Never exceed the maximum rated speed of 6000 RPM.
- Do not operate the centrifuge if vibration is observed.
